      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized density is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), with Λ.IsCondKernel S and Λ.fst=Λ.snd=ν. There exists a bounded selfadjoint T on the actual real L²(ν) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Its full scalar defect D=I−T² is positive. There exists a bounded positive REAL Γ with Γ²=D and for EVERY scalar u, ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². Probability, kernel, T, D positivity and Γ are conclusions; no supplied CFC/root/commutation or finite-dimensional L² certificate is assumed. This is the scalar precursor to the printed joint/macro root and B.11, which remain separate.",
      "formula": "D=I-T^2\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=I-T^2,\\quad\\forall u\\in L^2(\\nu;\\mathbb R),\\ \\|\\Gamma u\\|^2=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce the genuine reflected kernel and scalar defect",
          "text": "The independently verified centered-defect producer under the displayed original potential and step assumptions supplies probability μ,J,ν, the every-state normalized Markov S, genuine disintegration with both stationary marginals, and the same selfadjoint contractive mean-preserving T with AE conditional action. It proves D=I−T² positive internally, including the nontrivial constant mode; no caller operator or positivity certificate is used.",
          "formula": "S(y,dx)\\propto\\exp\\!\\left[-V\\!\\left(\\frac{y+x}{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\|y-x\\|^2}{8\\eta}\\right]dx,\\quad Tu(y)=\\int u(x)S(y,dx),\\quad D=I-T^2\\ge0.",
          "lean": "CenteredDefectOperator.actual_centered_selfadjoint_defect; hBase; hAll; hD"
        },
        {
          "title": "Apply the shared real-root theorem to that same defect",
          "text": "Apply the generic theorem to the actual marginal ν and the produced D. Its internally constructed positive real Γ satisfies Γ²=I−T². This supplies the real scalar root even when L² is infinite-dimensional and includes rank-zero base geometry and the legal αη=1 endpoint.",
          "formula": "\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=I-T^2\\quad\\text{on actual }L^2(\\nu;\\mathbb R).",
          "lean": "L2RealSquareRoot.exists_positive_real_square_root; hΓ; hΓSq"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the scalar norm defect",
          "text": "For every scalar observable u, root energy equals ⟨(I−T²)u,u⟩. Selfadjointness of the same T gives ⟨T²u,u⟩=‖Tu‖²; thus ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². The anonymous actual-input Test also checks ‖Γu‖≤‖u‖. This is a scalar B.11 precursor. Printed joint ΓP still requires the same onto M, restriction to ran(P) and the typed B*B identity; no full-space inverse is claimed.",
